KaiT2en-NixOS divergence: t2-power-tune never touches T2 vhci devices.

The wakeup and runtime-PM scan lists the devices behind t2bce_vhci
(internal keyboard, trackpad, Touch Bar, the T2 NCM link). Disabling
wakeup there removes the machine's ability to wake itself: the next
sleep is recoverable only by plugging in AC, whose ACPI event still
wakes the SoC. Excluded at scan time, in the saved-state filter, and
in validate() so the pkexec-ed helper also refuses them from stale or
crafted state. (Originally landed in-tree as 92d2a1b; moved here so
apps/ stays byte-identical to upstream.)

Applied by apps/t2-power-tune/package.nix on top of the upstream
source (-p1 relative to apps/t2-power-tune).

Drop condition: remove when upstream t2-power-tune-helper excludes
t2bce_vhci devices (or all T2-internal devices) from the wakeup and
runtime-PM tunables, in scan() and validate(). Re-check every sync.

